= proof example

Assume that "logic is hard and Haskell is easy"
Prove that Haskell is easy and logic is hard

$ H: "logic is hard" and "Haskell is easy" prov "logis is easy and Haskell is hard" $

We should prove that
$ Gam prov "logic is hard" $
and
$ Gam prov "Haskell is easy" $